STAGED ONLY (not built/installed). Proper fix: 8250_mtk is built-in (=y), so this needs a kernel rebuild + reboot.
Evidence: raw MMIO sweep on COM3 (NVDA0240:01) shows SAM EC replies cleanly only at 12.3..13.3 UART clocks/bit
for its 4,000,000-baud link => real UART input clock ~52 MHz, not the 26 MHz the driver assumes on ACPI.
Untested for COM1 (debug UART, _STA=0 here) and DGX Spark. With this applied, drop the surface_aggregator quirk.

--- a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_mtk.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_mtk.c
@@ static int mtk8250_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	uart.port.uartclk = clk_get_rate(data->uart_clk);
-	if (!uart.port.uartclk)
-		uart.port.uartclk = 26 * HZ_PER_MHZ;
+	if (!uart.port.uartclk) {
+		u32 freq;
+
+		/* ACPI: honour _DSD "clock-frequency"; NVIDIA N1X/GB10 UARTs run at 52 MHz. */
+		if (!device_property_read_u32(&pdev->dev, "clock-frequency", &freq) && freq)
+			uart.port.uartclk = freq;
+		else if (acpi_dev_hid_match(ACPI_COMPANION(&pdev->dev), "NVDA0240"))
+			uart.port.uartclk = 52 * HZ_PER_MHZ;
+		else
+			uart.port.uartclk = 26 * HZ_PER_MHZ;
+	}
